3. Protenix (transitive dependency)
-----------------------------------
ODesign builds on Protenix (https://github.com/bytedance/Protenix), Apache 2.0.


4. OpenFold (transitive dependency)
-----------------------------------
ODesign incorporates code from OpenFold
(https://github.com/aqlaboratory/openfold), licensed under Apache 2.0.
The vendored OpenFold pieces live under `src/utils/openfold_local/`.


5. ProteinMPNN (checkpoint + code)
----------------------------------
The protein invfold module uses weights from
https://github.com/dauparas/ProteinMPNN (MIT License).


6. LigandMPNN (checkpoint)
--------------------------
The `ligandmpnn_v_32_010_25.pt` checkpoint is from
https://files.ipd.uw.edu/pub/ligandmpnn/, by the Institute for Protein
Design, University of Washington (MIT License).


External tools NOT bundled
==========================

This fork does not bundle and does not require the following external tools.
They are referenced by gRNAde's secondary-structure code path; the fork
gracefully no-ops these calls when the tools aren't installed (Patch 11):

- X3DNA (https://x3dna.org/) — proprietary, academic-only, Linux/macOS only.
- EternaFold (https://eternagame.org/about/software) — academic license.

If you have either tool installed and want to use it, set the corresponding
env var (`X3DNA`, `ETERNAFOLD`) before launching ODesign and the original
codepaths will be exercised.


